why Every Alliance quest of Zul'Farrak in one run, lead-ins included.

# Zul'Farrak's Alliance quests in one guide: the pick-ups in Stormwind,
# Ironforge and Dalaran, Gryphon Master Talonaxe's chain in the Hinterlands
# and the Blasted Lands, Booty Bay, Dustwallow Marsh, Tanaris, the Shimmering
# Flats and Feralas (for Mages A Lesson in Literacy too), one run, then the
# hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over, so the guide picks up
# wherever the chain stands.
#
# The chains:
# - Gryphon Master Talonaxe's 2988 Witherbark Cages -> 2989 The Altar of Zul
#   -> 2990 Thadius Grimshade -> 2991 Nekrum's Medallion -> 2992 The
#   Divination.
# - Tabetha's Task 2861 (from Jennea Cannon) -> 2846 Tiara of the Deep.
# - Krazek's 2864 Tran'rek -> 2865 Scarab Shells; Trenton Lighthammer's 3042
#   Troll Temper; Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle's 2768 Divino-matic Rod.
# - Yeh'kinya's 3520 Screecher Spirits -> 3527 The Prophecy of Mosh'aru ->
#   4787 The Ancient Egg.
# - Klockmort Spannerspan's 2769 The Brassbolts Brothers -> 2770 Gahz'rilla.
# - Archmage Lan'dalock's 96770 The Witch Doctor's Head.
# - The OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon, a rare drop inside and in Tanaris, starts
#   351 Find OOX-17/TN! -> 648 Rescue OOX-17/TN! (an escort, then Booty Bay).
# - Mages: Garion Wendell's 82084 A Lesson in Literacy.
#
# Left out: 2993 Return to the Hinterlands and Saving Sharpbeak beyond it (the
# Hinterlands' story after 2992); 3528 The God Hakkar after The Ancient Egg
# (it needs the Sunken Temple, whose guide holds it); 3721 An OOX of Your Own
# (it needs the other two OOX chains); 8676 Wildmane the Elder (the Lunar
# Festival); the Rogues' 80411 The Talisman of Kazdor (not on the Codex page;
# its text asks for the job to be done alone, not in a group's run).
#
# Gahz'rilla comes only when someone rings the gong by the sacred pool
# with the Mallet of Zul'Farrak, and one mallet does it for the group.
# Qiaga the Keeper, an elite on top of the Altar of Zul, drops the Sacred
# Mallet; used at the altar at the very top of Jintha'Alor it becomes the
# Mallet. The guide passes Qiaga for The Altar of Zul anyway, so the Sacred
# Mallet is an optional goal there.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, Sergeant Bly or the graves
# inside, so their goals stand at the door (@38.7,20.1, Tanaris) with
# `group 5`. The bosses come in the order of the client's dungeon journal
# (Hydromancer Velratha, Gahz'rilla, Antu'sul, Theka the Martyr, Witch Doctor
# Zum'rah, Nekrum Gutchewer, Shadowpriest Sezz'ziz, Chief Ukorz Sandscalp),
# not of a recorded run. Every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a
# group that takes them in another order still gets each step ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The Tiara, the tablets, the scale, the head,
#   the medallion, the shells and the Troll Temper are quest items there: they
#   drop only while their quest is held. Sergeant Bly carries the rod.
# - The Mallet of Zul'Farrak: the Codex page's note on it (the gong, one
#   mallet per group, Qiaga, Jintha'Alor); the data has Qiaga, an elite of
#   level 50 at the Altar of Zul, drop the Sacred Mallet every time.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   44 to 54).
# - Lint warns that the door is more than 50 yards from the beacon's droppers
#   outside (in Tanaris and beyond); the optional goal stays at the door for
#   the ones inside.
# INGAME: where inside do Sergeant Bly and the Shallow Graves stand?

